  {
    "number": 441,
    "title": "Paint LIFX status from sessions with uncertain freshness (#439)",
    "body": "Refs #439. Found by the #22 installed trial.\n\n## Problem\n\n#20's rule made `highestStatus` return `unknown` whenever any shown root session had `uncertain` freshness, and the LIFX publisher paints nothing on `unknown`. Agent-state marks a session uncertain after five minutes without evidence, so a finished turn waiting to be read is nearly always uncertain. On the installed setup (hub 0.3.12, host `6b561ba`), 15 of 16 shown root sessions were uncertain, and `pendant-1` would have stayed unpainted in Work or Quiet.\n\n## Resulting behavior\n\n- `highestStatus` ranks every shown root session by the state the shared owner reports, whatever its freshness. It returns `unknown` only for an unavailable feed or a collector that isn't running. The owner chose this rule on 2026-09-26.\n- Everything else from #20 is unchanged: attention over working over done, done retired only by acknowledgment, silence never meaning done, transition-only painting, no replay, and no idle paint on an unavailable feed.\n- The Tidbyt uses `sessionState` and its own per-row uncertainty marker, so its code and tests are unchanged.\n- OpenSpec `gh-439-lifx-uncertain-freshness` is synced into `local-controller-host` and archived.\n\n## Acceptance evidence\n\nOn Node 24 from the worktree root.\n\n| Criterion | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| Uncertain sessions paint their state | `packages/agent-status/tests/status.test.mjs`: uncertain working, attention and done, plus restart-uncertain sessions, each keep their reported state. `controllers/lifx/tests/status-publisher.test.mjs`: a real owner with its clock moved 6 minutes past the evidence (every session `uncertain`) paints done green on Work entry, then blue at the next transition. Both tests failed before the fix (red confirmed) |\n| Unavailable feed still paints nothing | The existing `unknown` tests for an unavailable feed or a non-running collector, and the publisher's stale-input test, now retitled to what it covers |\n| Tidbyt unchanged | `test:tidbyt` (111 tests) and `test:tidbyt:python` (2 tests, run with Pillow in a disposable venv, because the host Python lacks it) |\n| Checks | At `da1c06c`: `build`, `typecheck`, `test:agent-status`, `test:lifx`, `test:local-controllers`, `test:tidbyt`, `test:contracts`, `test:contracts:python`, `test:package`, `test:mcp`, `test:hub`, `check:workflow`, `test:workflow`. At `5563ae5`, after merging main's #435 (Nanoleaf harness scripts only): `build`, `typecheck`, `test:agent-status:built`, `test:lifx:built`, `test:local-controllers:built`, `check:workflow`, `test:workflow` |\n\n## Risk\n\nA session that stopped without a delivered end stays working until it ends or reaches the 24-hour expiry, which is the Tidbyt's existing behavior. Free still stops painting. There's no wire, configuration or dashboard change.\n\n## Remaining\n\nIndependent reviews, Depot CI and merge. After merge, #22 installs the new host release and resumes its physical trial.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
